# ===== Target-specific extras =====
# fuzz_formatter-specific extras — whitespace / comment / trivia shapes
# the formatter must preserve-or-canonicalise. Splicing these into an
# otherwise valid statement is the fastest path to idempotence bugs.
#
# Note: libFuzzer's dictionary parser only accepts \xNN, \\, and \"
# escapes — not \n / \t / \r — so whitespace is spelled as \x09 / \x0a /
# \x0d throughout.

# Trailing trivia: whitespace only / comment only.
